est real Republican vulnerability, though the state's lean keeps this short of Likely D.", "watch": "Whether the $100M-plus pro-Paxton outside spending blitz moves the polls in the final weeks, or turnout patterns among young and suburban voters hold for Talarico.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: John Cornyn (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Texas's open Senate seat has become one of the cycle's marquee contests, with state Rep. James Talarico facing scandal-plagued Attorney General Ken Paxton after Paxton ousted incumbent John Cornyn in the primary. Recent polls from mid-to-late September show Talarico leading by roughly two to six points, with even some Republican-leaning pollsters showing the race tied or near-tied. Expert raters split between Tossup and Lean D, and prediction markets give Talarico about a 65% chance.\n\nTalarico holds a commanding financial advantage, having raised nearly $69 million to Paxton's $9 million, though Republican groups and Senate leadership have poured enormous sums into outside spending to prop up Paxton. The state's six-point Republican lean and a potentially tightening race keep this competitive, but the weight of polling and money favors Talarico heading into the final stretch.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6697, "margin": 2.08}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6924, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7255, "margin": 2.8}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6997, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6523, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6444, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6983, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7151, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.701, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7008, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.6832, "margin": 2.2}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7125, "margin": 2.5}]}